---
import CoursePage from "../../layouts/CoursePage.astro";
import { withBase } from "astro-theme-university/url";
import { sources } from "../../data/sources";
---
<CoursePage title="Keep the receipts." description="A small collection of useful evidence: fictional practice records, reusable worksheets and the original platform guidance." eyebrow="THE RESOURCE DESK">
  <section class="resources-section" id="practice-pack"><p class="eyebrow">01 / YOUR PRACTICE PACK</p><h2>Real skills. Fictional accounts.</h2><p class="reading-intro">These records are written for this course. Account aliases, amounts and outcomes are simulated. The reference date for the pack is 20 September 2026; apply the printed practice terms rather than guessing from today's date.</p>
  <div class="resource-downloads"><a class="button button-dark" href={withBase("/worksheets/receipt-pack.csv")} download>Download receipt pack <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a class="button button-outline" href={withBase("/worksheets/evidence-sheet.md")} download>Download evidence sheet <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>
  <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Practice receipts"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Record</th><th scope="col">Service</th><th scope="col">Biller / account</th><th scope="col">Printed terms</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">R01</th><td>STAY+</td><td>Apple / NORTH</td><td>A$12 monthly. Renews 8 October.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">R02</th><td>Mosaic Studio</td><td>Mosaic direct / NORTH</td><td>20 practice units monthly; annual commitment. Six payments remain. Practice exit charge: half the remaining balance.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">R03</th><td>Focus Paper</td><td>Google Play / SOUTH</td><td>A$8 monthly. Renews 8 October. Renewal currently active.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">R04</th><td>Notebook purchase</td><td>Campus Shop / NORTH</td><td>A$18, paid once. No continuing service.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
  </section>
  <section class="resources-section" id="dossiers"><p class="eyebrow">02 / WORKSHOP DOSSIERS</p><h2>Read what happened.</h2><div class="dossier-grid">
    <article class="dossier"><span class="micro">D01 / WEEKS 7 & 10</span><h3>Two plans. One request.</h3><p>Design plan: cancel requested. Stock plan: keep active. At 09:14 the design-plan request times out. At 09:18 the account returns confirmation C-204: design renewal off, paid access until 8 October. The stock plan remains active.</p><p>A 9 October invoice names the stock plan. It does not, on its own, show that the design-plan cancellation failed.</p></article>
    <article class="dossier"><span class="micro">N01 / WEEK 8</span><h3>The partner is the biller.</h3><p>The fictional Screen Club membership says “Billed through Campus Connect”. Campus Connect's supplied practice terms allow removal of the video add-on in its bundle settings; other bundle services remain active. Access to the removed add-on lasts until 31 October.</p><p>Use this record to practise the partner branch of the Netflix reading. Campus Connect is fictional.</p></article>
    <article class="dossier"><span class="micro">O01 / WEEK 9</span><h3>Before you accept the offer.</h3><p>Option A: pause until 8 November, then resume at 12 per month. Option B: 6 per month for two months, then 12, with a new six-month commitment. Option C: cancel renewal and retain already-paid access to 8 October.</p><p>Compare for two goals: “I no longer use it” and “I still need it but want a lower cost”. All amounts are practice units.</p></article>
    <article class="dossier"><span class="micro">S01 / WEEK 11</span><h3>The unresolved attempt.</h3><p>Focus Paper, Google Play, SOUTH. Request made 6 October at 18:40; a processing message is captured as E-01. No confirmation is supplied. Next scheduled renewal is 8 October. The goal is to establish whether renewal has actually been turned off.</p><p>Your message must ask for the missing outcome, not announce one.</p></article>
    <article class="dossier"><span class="micro">F01 / FINAL PRACTICAL</span><h3>Weekend Reader.</h3><p>Receipt F-01: Weekend Reader, billed by Apple to NORTH, A$9 per month, next renewal 3 November. The device is signed into SOUTH. The customer wants to prevent the next renewal and keep already-paid access.</p><p>E-02 is a failed attempt from SOUTH. E-03 is a later account record from NORTH: renewal off, paid access ending 3 November, confirmation WR-711. A separate newspaper plan remains active. Explain the appropriate route and which evidence supports the final conclusion.</p></article>
    <article class="dossier"><span class="micro">A REUSABLE METHOD</span><h3>Before / during / after.</h3><p><strong>Before:</strong> name the goal, biller, purchasing account and commitment.</p><p><strong>During:</strong> read the applicable terms and the effect of each choice.</p><p><strong>After:</strong> record the result, dates and supporting evidence. Label anything unresolved.</p><a class="text-link" href={withBase("/lab/")}>Practise the method ↗</a></article>
  </div></section>
  <section class="resources-section" id="sources"><p class="eyebrow">03 / READ THE ORIGINAL</p><h2>The source register.</h2><p class="reading-intro">Official instructions support the platform cases. Historical research supports the analysis. A source check means the linked public page was read on that date; it does not imply that a live account transaction was tested.</p><div class="source-register">{sources.map((source)=><details id={"source-"+source.id}><summary><span class="micro">{source.publisher}</span><span>{source.title}</span><span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p><strong>Use in this course:</strong> {source.use}</p><p><strong>Scope:</strong> {source.scope}</p><span class="checked-date">CHECKED {source.checked}</span><a class="text-link" href={source.url} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Read the original <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></details>)}</div></section>
</CoursePage>
